    </svg>
  </div>

  <!-- WHY THIS MATTERS -->
  <div class="why-matters">
    <h4>🌍 Why This Matters</h4>
    <p><strong>For Recommendation Systems:</strong> Real-time features (user viewing history, recent purchases) are critical for personalization. Without a feature store, computing these at serving time takes seconds, unacceptable for web latency. Feature stores pre-compute and cache, delivering in milliseconds.</p>
    <p><strong>For Fraud Detection:</strong> Fraud models must execute in real-time when a transaction occurs. They need features like account velocity and recent transaction patterns. These must be retrieved in tens of milliseconds. Feature stores enable this by caching hot features in Redis.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- KEY TAKEAWAY -->
  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Feature stores have two paths: batch (for training) and real-time (for serving)</li>
      <li>Batch features computed on schedule, stored in data warehouse</li>
      <li>Real-time features cached in low-latency databases (Redis, DynamoDB)</li>
      <li>Same feature API for both paths: models don't care about infrastructure</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

